WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
Texas Governor Greg Abbott is

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.736
pushing the state's parole board

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.270
to recommend a pardon

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.305
for a US Army

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.607
sergeant convicted of murder on Friday.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.542
Daniel Perry was convicted

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.510
of killing a protester

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.845
during a Black Lives Matter

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.546
rally back in 2020.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.081
He says he fired his weapon

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.316
in self-defense

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.250
after he says

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.585
protesters surrounded his car

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:21.087
as he drove through downtown Nashville.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.088
Lawyers argue

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.523
he had the right to open fire

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.624
after one demonstrator,

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.327
he says, raised an assault rifle at him.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.529
CNN's Camilla Bernal joins us now

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.597
with the latest.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.432
Camille, a very unusual case

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.600
to see a governor

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.667
weigh in so soon

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.635
right after this

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.872
whole matter was adjudicated in court.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.407
Yeah, this is not over,

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.608
but Governor Greg Abbott

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.143
is pointing to self-defense,

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.111
pointing to stand your ground laws

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.212
in Texas.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:46.579
And look,

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.481
there are some in conservative media

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.949
that have been encouraging

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:53.119
the governor to pardon Perry and even

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.422
Kyle Rittenhouse has been very vocal

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.156
on Twitter.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:58.024
Rittenhouse was acquitted

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.159
after he shot

00:00:59.159 --> 00:00:59.759
and killed

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.361
two people in Kenosha,

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:04.030
Wisconsin, during protests there.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.365
He's been asking for money

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.566
for the legal defense.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.835
He says he knows what this is all about.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.870
On the other hand, the Travis County

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.639
district attorney

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.473
speaking out

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.808
recently and saying

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.476
that this is very troubling

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:19.946
and saying that in the legal world,

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.981
it is a jury, not a governor,

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.583
who gets to decide this.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.617
That's a statement that we got

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.920
from Jose Garza of Travis County

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.255
very recently now, in terms of the case,

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.323
what happened here

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.826
was in 2020 in Austin, Texas.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.928
Daniel Perry is driving for

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.029
rideshare company

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.897
and he gets to the area

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.899
where all the protesters are.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.768
The key here is that he encounters

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.502
Garrett Foster,

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.337
who was 28 years old at the time.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.372
He was carrying an AK 47.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.240
And Perry's

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.009
defense says that Foster held up

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:50.743
or was

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.746
trying to essentially raise that AK 47.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.115
And that's when Perry felt

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.449
that his life was in jeopardy.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.150
He shot

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.651
and kill Foster,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.454
who you see there on your screen.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.723
So, yes, this is political.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.758
This is also in terms

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.693
of what happens

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.394
next part of the legal process.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.596
Because, look,

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.598
Perry has not been sentenced.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.700
He has not appealed his conviction.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.835
So this is really not over.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.370
And the family

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.304
of Garrett

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.007
Foster reacting after that verdict

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.076
on Friday. Here is his father

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.980
just like to say, we're

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.648
thankful for the legal team

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:31.985
that represented us and the jury

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.888
and we're happy with the verdict.

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:35.822
We are

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.858
very sorry for his family as well.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.094
Just there's no winners in this.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:44.797
And I'm just glad it's over.

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:46.065
Now, Governor Greg

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.067
Abbott is asking for this process

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.869
to go quickly, to be expedited.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:50.803
We'll see what happens.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:51.137
Of course,

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.473
there is going to be a lot of opposition

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.041
on the side of the DEA

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:55.642
and those

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:56.276
who are

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:56.910
really trying

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.578
to support the foster family

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.180
through all of this, Jim.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.414
So let's discuss

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:02.682
this very unusual case

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:03.783
with former federal prosecutor

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.118
Michael Zeldin.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:06.219
Michael, good to see you.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.221
What is your reaction to Governor

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.022
Abbott's announcement

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.456
that he is working

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.524
to pardon

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.226
this man just one day

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.594
after he was convicted of murder?

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.262
As Kamilah was saying a few moments ago,

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.597
he hasn't even been sentenced yet.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.233
That's right.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:20.633
And you have to

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.468
understand the context of this.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:23.169
This Sergeant

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.471
Perry is 70 miles away from his base,

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.674
driving around in an

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:29.342
Uber car of some sort

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.377
He encounters these protesters.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.279
And rather than turn around and leave,

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.647
he drives his car

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:35.548
into the middle of them.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.217
And you can't forget Charlottesville,

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.918
where people were killed by a car

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.486
doing the exact same thing.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.389
So as he's approached by the victim,

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.924
instead of,

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.159
again, leaving the scene

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:48.995
as he could have, he opens fire on him.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.263
The jury deliberated

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:53.266
17 hours, Jim, over an eight day trial.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.300
And they convicted of murder.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.170
They reject his

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.739
right to defend himself defense.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.275
And the judge and Governor Abbott

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:05.011
should let the jury's verdict stand.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:08.214
There's no basis in law or fact for this.

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:08.781
So it

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.317
therefore smacks of politics

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.253
because this was a Black Lives

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.555
Matter protest and you can't ignore

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:16.889
that context.

